# Conventional placeholder MAC used in iWRAP log fixtures (not a device address)
00:11:22:33:44:55

# Key-independent sha256 of the images make image builds locally from the stock file + this repository
# (reproducible digests, no key: the OTA key bytes are neutralised before hashing - see the file).
file:result/stockfw/ARTIFACTS.md

# stock-text:<regex> - a text string (>= 48 B) shared with the stock file that is an interface fact; full match
# after stripping surrounding white space.  Text strings shorter than 48 B are never reported; binary runs only
# through a byte-exact stock-bin entry (end of this file).
# Bluegiga iWRAP command / event lines (the Bluetooth module's public command set, iWRAP User Guide): the
# firmware has to send and parse the same text the stock firmware does.
stock-text:(SET|LIST|CALL|CLOSE|KILL|RING|INQUIRY|PAIR|CONNECT|NO CARRIER|AUDIO|A2DP|AVRCP|STREAMING|SSP|BATTERY|HFP|VOLUME)\b[ -~]*
stock-text:[A-Z0-9_ .-]*\b(I2S_SLAVE|JOINT_STEREO|AUTOCALL|AVRCP|A2DP|PAGEMODE|CODEC)\b[A-Z0-9_ .-]*
# Character-set tables: the Base64 alphabet (and its pieces).
stock-text:[A-Z]*[a-z]*[0-9]*[+/]*=*
# White space runs (display padding).
stock-text:\s*

# stock-bin:<path> <offset> <length> <sha256> - ONE binary run shared with the stock file, named byte for byte: the
# finding must be in that file at that offset with that length, and its bytes must hash to the sha256.  Anything
# else (a changed byte, a longer run, another offset or file) still fails.  Keep this list as short as possible.
# (none: ota_loader_v4's stage-0 cache sync is written so that it shares no 16-byte run with the stock file - the
# retired ota_loader_v3 needed one entry for its D-cache clean loop)
